00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.870
You've all used TCP,
that's for sure.

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:47.170
And the C in TCP
stands for congestion.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:50.500
And there's an algorithm that
if you went through school

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:53.390
to learn these things, you
might remember how it works.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:54.760
And it's really complicated.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:56.290
And not only is it
very complicated,

00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:59.540
but on the same time, it's
not incredibly performing.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.780
There's a little
bit of a problem.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.850
It has a long time
to actually get

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:06.250
to use the whole
bandwidth of a network,

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:09.280
because it starts by basically
uploading little by little.

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:12.024
And that's, among other things,
why, for instance, Chrome,

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:13.690
rather than having a
one TCP connection,

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:16.820
establishes six of them
to avoid these problems.

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:19.300
Now, the thing is that
that algorithm was not

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.220
the only possible solution.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:23.720
And someone came up
with a new solution.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:26.830
So there's a new congestion
algorithm for TCP.

00:03:26.830 --> 00:03:30.220
It's called BBR, which stands
for Bottleneck Bandwidth

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:32.320
and Roundtrip Propagation Time.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.250
And basically the only thing--

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.380
MARK MANDEL: Propogation
time is silent.

00:03:36.380 --> 00:03:39.250
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah, BBRPT.

00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:42.490
The whole idea is
that it's still TCP.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:43.540
It looks like TCP.

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:45.090
You use it like TCP.

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:48.880
But it will make it so it
uses better the bandwidth

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.170
that it is allowed to
use, which is really cool.

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:52.190
MARK MANDEL: Awesome.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:54.934
